{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment","id":987037,"title":"Advantage of Hedgespun Raiment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T18:43:26-07:00","id":987037,"title":"Advantage of Hedgespun Raiment","content":"So, this is a question I've had since 1e changeling, and going into 2e I figure it's something I'd like to figure out. Hedgespun Raiment, at it's most basic (not enhanced with extra defense or what have you), is basically clothes, armor, etc. With changelings, it grants a +2 equipment bonus to social interactions - which is cool, but also something you could do with normal clothes. Armor that is hedgespun is vulnerable to iron. It's also very notably armor.<br /> <br /> So what's the advantage of spending a merit dot for hedgespun armor? If your armor is just going to show up as flak armor or football gear, why not just get flak armor? I mean, I know if you take extra dots being that initial payment you can make it clothes + or armor +, for bonuses to init/speed/defense, but from where I'm standing it seems like it'd be safer to have normal flak armor (as that doesn't have the weakness of iron), and oddly enough less likely to draw the eyes of someone than if your unlucky enough that your fae plate mail looks like football gear. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T20:23:38-07:00","id":987075,"title":"","content":"It is sometimes rather difficult to find pants fitted for digitigrade legs or helmets that will accommodate a small rack of elk horns.<br /> <br /> Additionally, appearances go pretty far, especially with the fae; it doesn't much matter that your armor wrought of violet flame looks like a questionably-designed sporting uniform to mortal eyes when you're half a mile into the boiler room Hedge chatting with a hobgoblin devil-count whose greatest fear is that the Tyrian Lord of Ashes will seek an audience with him.<br /> <br /> It's fancy kit for fae encounters and not many people go around with iron weapons these days anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T22:33:14-07:00","id":987105,"title":"","content":"Yeah okay, I can see that. Sort of something that might stop questions of why your pants have an extra long angle or your helmet has holes in it, should they see it without you actually wearing it? It still seems a strange thing to require to purchase with merit dots / experience, rather than simply giving to it based on availability like other sets of equipment (at least, the hedgespun raiment that mimics said equipment - if it's -better- than them I see the need to pay), but that does make a sort of sense. Far as the iron weapons, that was more a note of consideration against things like changelings and hunters - not many people go around in football gear outside either, and I'd at least find it odd if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:06:59-07:00","id":987178,"title":"","content":"I thiiiiiiiink Tokens gotten in play will be habdled like fetishes amd not cost dots. Don't quote me on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:54:56-07:00","id":991075,"title":"","content":"In the last game I played(1E), we had a house rule that all hedgespun automatically possessed the same stats as it's mundane equivalent. This encouraged players to craft interesting gear via hedgespinning or use their Resources to purchase cool &quot;0-dot&quot; stuff from one of the freehold's artisans, rather than simply crafting/purchasing normal equipment. If a player spent xp on the Hedgespun merit, they could then add a bonus per dot. Our house rule was very similar to the rules written for 2E, except that the hedgespun possessed normal stats without spending a dot on the merit. You could adopt a similar house rule if you think that dropping xp on hedgespun raiment seems rather pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:51:07-07:00","id":991135,"title":"","content":"Techically you can add an equiptment bonus to Hedge Rainments, so say you have Hedgespun Token \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, you spend one dot on making it Hedgespun rainments and the rest to an equiptment bonus, +4 that you can use for social roles, because you look fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:09:06-07:00","id":991161,"title":"","content":"That's true, and I understand if the first dot of the merit is intended to be the &quot;price of admission&quot; for hedgespun, but it just seems kinda useless to me. According to the rules as written so far, one dot hedgespun(such as a blade of moonlight or a dress of snowflakes) only gains the ability to exist. That's it. Most of the players in my last game agreed that it seemed rather foolish to dump xp on equipment that was only cosmetically magical rather than simply purchase the mundane equivalent with their Resources merit(compared to other merits that grant a tangible benefit). We really liked the storytelling potential of 'lings running around with knives of frozen flame or caps knitted out of children's fears(even if they granted no mechanical benefits), so we agreed to make the rules for hedgespun less restrictive and it led to some pretty cool stories. I'm just saying that compared to other merits, I can see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a>'s point. Perhaps the benefit of Gossamer Raiment could extend to all hedgespun, so that a one dot hedgespun sword cobbled from nightmares would be treated as a normal blade during combat, but give a bonus to Intimidation rolls against other fae. Otherwise, the one dot version of any hedgespun just seems rather pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:35:42-07:00","id":991169,"title":"","content":"The one dot surcharge is *cheap* for what you can get with Hedgespun Raiment. You are better off forging weapons from the Hedge. They can trivially have a damage bonus of 5 and trigger the catch for the +2L damage contract. Its also cosmetically magical.<br /> <br /> On that note, equipment and clothes forged from the Hedge is probably your best bet for free cosmetically magical gear. Proper hedgespun raiment only offers the social bonus--probably for being super posh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 10-21-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:03:08-07:00","id":991178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hedgebound Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=991075#post991075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the last game I played(1E), we had a house rule that all hedgespun automatically possessed the same stats as it's mundane equivalent. This encouraged players to craft interesting gear via hedgespinning or use their Resources to purchase cool &quot;0-dot&quot; stuff from one of the freehold's artisans, rather than simply crafting/purchasing normal equipment. If a player spent xp on the Hedgespun merit, they could then add a bonus per dot. Our house rule was very similar to the rules written for 2E, except that the hedgespun possessed normal stats without spending a dot on the merit. You could adopt a similar house rule if you think that dropping xp on hedgespun raiment seems rather pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough I made similar house rules, though mine were more towards the end that if you spent dots with for hedgespun items, it's treated the same way that having a kith that grants armor or having the lethal mein merit would - which is to say, just removing the statement that their mask cannot be mistaken for anything other than a weapon / armor. Back then though you were paying a whole three dots for armor that just did... well, what armor did. I -THINK- in 2e they reduced the cost so there is at least that, but it always seemed odd to me that hedgespun material was so... noticable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=991135#post991135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Techically you can add an equiptment bonus to Hedge Rainments, so say you have Hedgespun Token \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, you spend one dot on making it Hedgespun rainments and the rest to an equiptment bonus, +4 that you can use for social roles, because you look fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem that I'd ultimately have with this is... if I spent those merits towards resources, I'd similarly get equipment bonuses for the high quality items I could use for whatever purpose; and, that bonus would not extend to that one item, but whatever I bought. Now; Ultimately its two different merits with two different goals in mind, but equipment bonuses / social bonuses are fairly easy to gather, in my experience.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:47:05-07:00","id":991354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=991169#post991169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one dot surcharge is *cheap* for what you can get with Hedgespun Raiment. You are better off forging weapons from the Hedge. They can trivially have a damage bonus of 5 and trigger the catch for the +2L damage contract. Its also cosmetically magical.<br /> <br /> On that note, equipment and clothes forged from the Hedge is probably your best bet for free cosmetically magical gear. Proper hedgespun raiment only offers the social bonus--probably for being super posh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's only &quot;cheap&quot; if you buy more than one dot. I guess maybe I just really liked the take on hedgespun in Goblin Markets, and saw no reason for players to spend xp on something that was 100% cosmetic. I can't think of another merit that has the same built in &quot;surcharge&quot; and gives no mechanical benefit for purchasing only one dot. So, back to the point of the original post, I can see how making mundane purchases with a single dot of resources would seem like a bargain compared to dropping a dot in hedgespun.<br /> <br /> I also understand that we have only seen scenes from the &quot;rough cut&quot; of the 2E rules so far, but I would really like a clear line to be drawn between tokens and hedgespun. There is a tiny disconnect between the rules we have seen regarding &quot;hedgespun raiment&quot;(which clearly states that there are no mechanical benefits for one dot) and the write up for the token &quot;gossamer raiment&quot;(which has a +2 social bonus and a different catch), yet they also make reference to each other as if they are supposed to be the same thing. I'm not sure if they are meant to be two totally different things or not, but my understanding was that all hedgespun would be items crafted by changelings that would be &quot;always on&quot; and would not require activation(and thus have no need for a catch). I found the whole hedgespun/token rules of 1E fairly confusing(and hard to explain to players), so I wish they would be firmly two different things in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:22:34-07:00","id":991364,"title":"","content":"For something free you can hedge warp some weird clothes together, with the only down side that when you where them outside of the Hedge you have to spend a Glamour per day to maintain them as long as its outside the hedge (put them back in the Hedge and they don't have to be maintained).<br /> <br /> Which makes sense Hedgespun is object, its not alive, but a Hedgewarped IS alive, its actually a living piece of the Hedge you transformed and so has to be fed.<br /> <br /> So Hedgespun Rainments don't have to be fed, you can just hang it up in your closet. It also has a mask of its own to humans won't freak out seeing it. Downside is it costs merit dots to purchase, unless maybe you focus a session on making it, because stuff aquired in play doesn't require merits to have (but also isn't protected by sacity of merits then).<br /> <br /> Hedgewarped Rainment (for lack of a better term), have to be fed glamour, in the Hedge that just happens, but Ironside you have to fed it a Glamour per day. Plus no mask, so if you make something freaky like a suit out of cosmic star filled space, people can see that and they will be all WTF?<br /> <br /> This can be more akward if you Hedge Warp a person in to being and take them Ironside and for to feed them glamour. It'd just be bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T00:35:55-07:00","id":993929,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that I always found it weird to have to pay a merit dot to simply get an item of mundane quality. It's additional dots that make the gear interesting. I guess you could argue that normal gear cannot be upgraded over time, as Raiment can with more XP-costs.<br /> <br /> I am not just sure why it's considered <u><b>mechanically interesting</b></u> to have to pay the first dot of XP just to make the item function as it should. Shouldn't even the weakest tokens be something out of the ordinary? Even the weakest tokens did have effects, like Bonecomb, The murmuring coin, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T01:01:19-07:00","id":993933,"title":"","content":"Important thing to consider: dots do not just represent Experience costs.<br /> <br /> Hedgespun is made through Hedgespinning and lower-dot stuff is easier to put together (and thus less Glamour intensive to make).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T05:41:28-07:00","id":994000,"title":"","content":"Honestly simple Hedge Spun rainments without mechanically benifits should cost 0 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:53:15-07:00","id":994047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=994000#post994000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly simple Hedge Spun rainments without mechanically benifits should cost 0 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. &quot;You can have a simple cosmetic piece of Hedgespun like a hat or a pair of glasses without any dots&quot; was a thing in 1e and you'll notice that the one-dot version represents an entire <i>outfit.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:29:50-07:00","id":994065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=993929#post993929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree that I always found it weird to have to pay a merit dot to simply get an item of mundane quality. It's additional dots that make the gear interesting. I guess you could argue that normal gear cannot be upgraded over time, as Raiment can with more XP-costs.<br /> <br /> I am not just sure why it's considered <u><b>mechanically interesting</b></u> to have to pay the first dot of XP just to make the item function as it should. Shouldn't even the weakest tokens be something out of the ordinary? Even the weakest tokens did have effects, like Bonecomb, The murmuring coin, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=993933#post993933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important thing to consider: dots do not just represent Experience costs.<br /> <br /> Hedgespun is made through Hedgespinning and lower-dot stuff is easier to put together (and thus less Glamour intensive to make).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987037-advantage-of-hedgespun-raiment?p=994000#post994000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly simple Hedge Spun rainments without mechanically benifits should cost 0 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>And agree.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the powers-that-be would consider modifying the hedgespinning rules to state that it requires three successes to create a basic(0-dot) outfit of hedgespun(raiment) or a single item with properties identical to it's mundane equivalent(tool/weapon/what-have-you) with the usual &quot;Ironside Drawback&quot;, but no supernatural benefits other than a Mask to conceal it's true nature. Then, if desired, supernatural enhancements could be added for an additional three hedgespinning successes per dot. This way, you could unambiguously craft or acquire hedgespun that adds some &quot;fairy tale flavor&quot; without being concerned with purchasing a merit for it unless it provides some mechanical benefit above and beyond normal equipment. I feel like this would dovetail rather nicely with mundane crafting rules while at the same time eliminating the feeling that you are wasting xp on an underwhelming one dot merit. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","user":"Hedgebound Heart","date":". 10-27-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}